# LF everywhere, on every platform. This branch is read and diffed far more than it is edited, and the
# knowledge base under unity/agent/kb is written by the agent's Python as UTF-8 without BOM and LF and
# read back byte-for-byte — a CRLF checkout would leave every file permanently modified in the eyes of
# `git status`, which is the drift detector the whole pipeline leans on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# NO GIT LFS ON THIS BRANCH. Deliberately.
#
# The working repositories track 3.2 GB of textures, meshes, audio and FBX through LFS. None of that
# is here (see README.md), so none of the LFS filters are either — a pattern kept without the objects
# behind it hands a fresh clone a file full of pointer text where it expected a PNG.
#
# One consequence worth knowing: adding a binary asset to this branch stores it as an ordinary blob.
# That is fine at this size and stops being fine quickly. Assets belong on the working repositories.

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.exr  binary

*.cs   text diff=csharp
*.py   text diff=python
